answer:
Substitute $x = 4$ into the expression:

\begin{align*}
&(3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\
\Rightarrow&(3(4)-2)(4(4)+1)-(3(4)-2)4+1\\
\Rightarrow&(12-2)(16+1)-(12-2)4+1\\
\Rightarrow&10 \cdot 17 - 10 \cdot 4 + 1\\
\Rightarrow&170 - 40 + 1\\
\Rightarrow&130 + 1\\
\Rightarrow&\boxed{131}
\end{align*}

First, simplify the expression:
\begin{align*}
(3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1 &= (3x-2)((4x+1)-4x+1) \\
&= (3x-2)(1) \\
&= 3x-2
\end{align*}

Now, substitute $x = 4$ into the simplified expression:
\begin{align*}
3x-2 &= 3(4)-2 \\
&= 12-2 \\
&= 10
\end{align*}

Thus, the value of the expression when $x = 4$ is $\boxed{10}$.

